# Rate-accuracy verification. Light channel only -- no audio cable needed.
#
# The 10 Hz block comes FIRST on purpose: it raises the flicker ISR tick to
# 10 x LED_FLICKER_TICK_MULT = 2500 Hz (400 us), and the tick is never lowered
# within a session, so every later block is measured on that same 400 us grid.
#
# Predicted OLD error (period rounded up to a whole number of 400 us ticks):
#    10 Hz  100000/400 = 250.00 -> 250  ->  10.00000 Hz   exact
#     7 Hz  142857/400 = 357.14 -> 358  ->   6.98324 Hz   -0.240%   <- measured 6.98320
#     8 Hz  125000/400 = 312.50 -> 313  ->   7.98722 Hz   -0.160%
#     9 Hz  111111/400 = 277.78 -> 278  ->   8.99281 Hz   -0.080%
#     6 Hz  166667/400 = 416.67 -> 417  ->   5.99520 Hz   -0.080%
#
# With the phase-locked origin all five should now read exact.
# 100% white 600 ms marker at t=0 is the sync reference on the light channel.
0 40 50 100 255 255 255 15
600 0 50 0 0 0 0 15
1000   10 50 80 0 0 255 15     # 10 Hz, 60 s  (sets the 400 us tick)
61000   7 50 80 0 0 255 15     #  7 Hz, 60 s  (the worst case)
121000  8 50 80 0 0 255 15     #  8 Hz, 60 s
181000  9 50 80 0 0 255 15     #  9 Hz, 60 s
241000  6 50 80 0 0 255 15     #  6 Hz, 60 s
301000 10 50 0 0 0 0 15        # off  -> 5 min 1 s total
